notes:
DNS (Domain name system) - Attaches names to IP addresses.
Domain hierarchy - Right to left order in the domain name systems.
  Root domain - "." Just the period.
  TLD (Top-level domain) - The most righthand part of a domain name like .com . Splits into two types.
    gTLD (Generic top level) - Used to show what the TLD is for like edu = education, org = organisation.
    ccTLD (Country code top level domain) - Used for geographical purposes, for example .ca for sites based in Canada.
  Second-level domain - The name of the DNS, for example github. Limited to 63 characters and also a-z, 0-9 and hyphens (cannot start or end with hyphens or have consecutive hyphens.)
  Subdomain - Sits on the left-hand side of the Second-level domain, for example admin. .
    Subdomain limits - Same restriction as Second-level domain. Can create multiple subdomains to create longer names 253 character limit.

    
